id: pm-fr6u17
title: "GH-937: package list exposes alias rows as packages and overstates the catalog total"
description: "pm package list emits one row per resolvable alias while naming the collection and details.total as packages. Packages with multiple aliases therefore appear twice, inflate the catalog count, and invite agents to repeat installs."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:packages","area:sdk",contracts,counting
created_at: "2026-08-08T14:06:01.280Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-08T14:06:01.280Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Each package is represented once with a deterministic aliases collection, or the row kind and counts explicitly distinguish aliases from packages; SDK, CLI, JSON, TOON, and human outputs agree; agents can iterate packages without duplicate installs; temporary-workspace acceptance and exact coverage prove the contract"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make package discovery semantically truthful and safe for agent iteration
value: Package authors retain flexible aliases while consumers receive one unambiguous catalog cardinality
why_now: GH-937 demonstrated generated consumers already repeat the inflated catalog count
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: pm CLI 2026.8.5 and current first-party package registry
repro_steps: Initialize a temporary workspace and run pm package list --json; compare entries.length and distinct package_name count. The current catalog returns 15 rows for 13 packages because governance-audit and digital-twin each have two aliases.
expected_result: "The package collection and total represent unique packages while preserving all resolvable aliases, or the contract explicitly names alias rows and separately reports alias_count and package_count."
actual_result: The response reports details.total=15 and returns duplicate package rows for a 13-package catalog without disclosing alias indexing.
component: package catalog SDK and CLI projection
